I only asked two rules questions of Christopher over the weekend and I know this was hotly debated somewhere [s]but I can&#39;t remember which thread (and searching for &quot;play&quot; would be useless).[/s] It was debated in [url=https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/the-shortest-possible-game-3594 ]this thread.[/url] 

&nbsp;

If (card A) says &quot;Play a card&quot; on it, it does not go to the discard pile until after the card played by that card is resolved.

e.g. 3 Burst cards in trash. Play Fleet of Foot, draw Light Speed Barrage, play&nbsp; Light Speed Barrage, the damage will be 3. Put&nbsp;  Light Speed Barrage in discard pile, put&nbsp;  Fleet of Foot&nbsp;  in discard pile. 

&nbsp;

 EDIT:&nbsp;  If (card A) says &quot;Play a card&quot; on it, it does not go to the discard pile until (card B) is resolved, if (card B) also&nbsp;  says &quot;Play a card&quot; (card A) will only go to the discard pile after both (card C) and (card B) are resolved and (card B) will only go to the discard pile after (card C) is resolved.
